{
  "_doc": "normalize_painting_state (Python) and normalizePaintingState (JS) read `painting` the same (docs/scene-state-v2.md, `painting`): `version` is always 1. The z_index of a group or raster object is the first finite JSON number (not a boolean, not text) of `z_index`, then `zIndex`; an integer too large for a double is not finite. Without one, it is the item's place among the groups (raster objects). A group's is rounded as Math.round (halves toward +infinity), a raster object's is kept; both are at least 0. Only these fields are compared: the editor also reads a group's `locked`, which Python omits.",
